.SH CONFIGURATION
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mergewright/config.toml, in TOML. Every key is optional. An
unknown key is a warning, not an error; a value a key does not take stops mwr
with the line and column.
.SS [ui]
.TP
.B theme
The colour theme. auto follows the terminal's background, dark if it does not
say.
.br
Values: auto | dark | light | high-contrast. Default: "auto".
.TP
.B icons
Glyphs: plain works in every font; nerd needs a Nerd Font.
.br
Values: plain | nerd. Default: "plain".
.TP
.B overview
Start with the overview strip shown. O still toggles it.
.br
Values: true | false. Default: false.
.SS [graph]
.TP
.B renderer
How the graph is drawn. auto uses what the terminal says it can do.
.br
Values: auto | pixel | unicode | ascii. Default: "auto".
.TP
.B default_branch
The branch that owns the leftmost lane. Unset: detected.
.br
Values: any branch name. Default: (unset).
.TP
.B max_lanes
Lanes drawn before the rest fold behind +N. Unset: 8, 10 or 12 by terminal
width.
.br
Values: any number from 2 up. Default: (unset).
.TP
.B merged_branches
folded: a merged branch sits behind its merge; space opens it. shown: every
branch on its own lane. Unset: folded. A bad value is a problem, not an error.
Picking a mode under GRAPH MODE in ? writes this key (the only one Mergewright
writes).
.br
Values: folded | shown. Default: (unset).
.SS [diff]
.TP
.B context
Lines of context around each change.
.br
Values: any number of lines. Default: 3.
.TP
.B ignore_whitespace
Hide whitespace-only changes.
.br
Values: true | false. Default: false.
.TP
.B word_tint
Tint the changed words inside a changed line.
.br
Values: true | false. Default: true.
.SS [radar]
.TP
.B foxtrot
Mistake Radar: a merge on the default branch that rewrote its first-parent
history.
.br
Values: default | off | info | warning. Default: "default".
.TP
.B backward
Mistake Radar: the default branch merged into a feature branch.
.br
Values: default | off | info | warning. Default: "default".
.TP
.B accidental-pull
Mistake Radar: a branch merged with its own remote copy, as git pull leaves.
.br
Values: default | off | info | warning. Default: "default".
.TP
.B evil
Mistake Radar: a merge carrying changes neither parent had.
.br
Values: default | off | info | warning. Default: "default".
.TP
.B duplicate
Mistake Radar: the same patch on several branches.
.br
Values: default | off | info | warning. Default: "default".
.TP
.B force-pushed
Mistake Radar: a remote-tracking branch that was force-pushed.
.br
Values: default | off | info | warning. Default: "default".
.TP
.B risky-state
Mistake Radar: a detached HEAD, or unpushed commits on the default branch.
.br
Values: default | off | info | warning. Default: "default".
.SS [keys]
.TP
.B suspend_on_ctrl_z
ctrl+z suspends Mergewright like any terminal program; undo keeps u.
.br
Values: true | false. Default: false.
.SS [keys.<context>]
.TP
.B <action>
Rebind an action. The context and action names are in KEYS.
.br
Values: one key, a list of keys, or "none". Default: (the KEYS table).
.SS [theme.<kind>]
.TP
.B <token>
Override one colour of the dark, light or high-contrast theme. Lane colours are
fixed.
.br
Values: "#RRGGBB". Default: (the built-in theme).
.br
Kinds: dark, light, high-contrast. Tokens: bg, surface, surface-raised,
selection, border, text, text-muted, accent, added, removed, warning, info,
ours, theirs, open, ours-tint, theirs-tint, open-tint, role-this, role-under,
role-trunk, role-other.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the config folder is: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mergewright. Ignored unless
absolute; unset, $HOME/.config is used.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Where crash reports go: $XDG_STATE_HOME/mergewright. Unset or empty,
$HOME/.local/state is used.
.TP
.B HOME
The fallback for both of the above. With neither it nor XDG_CONFIG_HOME set, no
config file is read, and mwr says so.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to anything non-empty: no colour is drawn. Shape, weight and glyphs still
tell things apart.
.TP
.B TERM, COLORTERM, TERM_PROGRAM
Read, with TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION, KITTY_WINDOW_ID, TMUX, SSH_TTY, SSH_CONNECTION
and the terminal's own answers, to choose the rendering tier and colour depth.
graph.renderer overrides the tier.
.TP
.B MWR_PERF_TRACE
A file name: every drawn frame appends one line to it, for a performance report.
.TP
.B MWR_ASKPASS_SOCKET
Set by mwr for the git it runs, so that git can ask mwr for a password. Not for
setting by hand.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mergewright/config.toml
The config file; see CONFIGURATION. No file is the normal case.
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mergewright/recent
The repositories opened recently, offered when mwr starts outside one.
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mergewright/launches
Launches counted, so the line saying where help is shows on the first five, or
until you first open the command palette.
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/mergewright/
Crash reports.
.TP
.B <git directory>/mergewright/
Per repository: the undo journal (undo-journal.jsonl), the pane layout, a paused
rewrite's plan, the message file ctrl+e opens in your editor, and whether you
declined the commit-graph offer.
